    energy_reserve_coopt: { cell: "I", ev: "SPP-55 (2026-09-07, ZERO LP — the arm was killed at the pre-solve half of its pre-registered STOP gate; no screen, no control, nothing registered, keeper-3 UNCHANGED; PRECOMMIT-spp-55-2026-09-07.md, FINDING-spp-55-2026-09-07.md, docs/handoffs/spp55/): I — INERT. THE SPP ENTRY NOW EXISTS under this shared gate (model/reserves/spec.py::_spp_design, the MISO-RBDC template, NO new field): ONE BAA-wide Contingency Reserve family on SPP's OWN published Contingency Reserve Demand Curve (Protocols v119 §4.1.5(1)(a)/§4.1.5.2: scarcity factor 0.25/0.5/1.0 x ($1,000 + $100) = $275/$550/$1,100 per MW — corroborated to the dollar by the posted RTBM MCPs, which sit at exactly 275/550/1,100 in every 2023-2025 short interval; the charter's $250 spin VRL is a CAP on the spin sub-constraint and the $50,000 power-balance VRL is the energy slack's relaxation cap, neither a demand-curve step), requirement = 0.964 x 1.2 x hourly MSSC (RSG Operating Process 0820EXT00002 §4.1-4.3: largest single unit >= 600 MW x availability; Wolf Creek 1 -> 1,500 MW vs SPP's posted cleared 1,514/1,484 MW medians, model/measured 0.983/0.961). Six published constants, one MEASURED share, zero tuned. MEASURED FOOTPRINT: 140/117/109 five-minute short intervals in 68/45/37 events of median length ONE interval; 4/3/7 hour-long shortage hours; and 1/0/0 of the 42/59/68 C3c hours coincide with ANY reserve shortage (reserve-short hours price at a median $32-36). PRE-SOLVE GATE: keeper-3's reserve-eligible headroom is below the 1.5 GW requirement in 0/1/0 hours (min 2,884/1,169/2,399 MW; 3.4-17x the requirement inside the measured window) — the row can bind in NO measured shortage hour of any year (leg (i)(a) = 0.00, bar 0.50), so under rule 29 step 0 no LP was spent. STRUCTURAL READING: SPP's reserve scarcity is a 5-minute ramp/capacity object an hourly perfect-foresight LP without a deliverability bound clears out of 6-18 GW of slow-unit headroom (the miso-38 gate-4 lesson on SPP's own data); making the family LIVE is SPP-56's deliverability question (R-22), and C3c is a 5-minute RT price-formation object no hourly lever reaches (R-21). Re-test condition: a 10-minute ramp bound on the held MW that brings DELIVERABLE headroom below the requirement in the measured 4/3/7 hours (computable at zero LP with docs/handoffs/spp55/headroom.py) — never this family alone re-armed. PRIOR: SPP-21 seed U (no verdict minted)." },
