    offer_curve_by_group: { cell: "K", ev: "SPP-52a: R -> O -> K. PROMOTED TO KEEPER 2026-09-10 BY OWNER RULING in-session ('Determine if spp 52a should have been promoted. If so, promote...'), so the O this lane deliberately left open -- 'O not K because PROMOTION IS THE OWNER'S ACT and has not been ruled' -- is now RESOLVED. The promoting session re-scored BOTH this run and keeper 4 from their committed artifacts before ruling and verified every carve-out condition against the run's own run_config.json rather than taking the producing lane's word: it STRICTLY DOMINATES keeper 4 (C3a and C3b both FAIL -> PASS, C1's single failing row -8.23 -> -8.13 TWh, nothing gated worse; per year 2025 NOT-YET -> CALIBRATED-WITH-CAVEATS). The determination is UNCHANGED at NOT-YET and the reported-only D-A diurnal amplitude falls ~2 pp, both reported rather than netted. Rule 1 [R-STRUCT]'s first half is not engaged: the run carries EXACTLY keeper 4's structure, so no structure was traded for level, and the flat-to-0.12-pp level response CONFIRMS the price-family lane's G-2 steepening refusal rather than overturning it. Record: docs/calibration-log/spp.md (spp-20). ORIGINAL LANE RECORD, preserved as written EXCEPT that two of its figures are SUPERSEDED and flagged here rather than silently rewritten (keeper-audit, 2026-09-10, reproducing the scorer at full precision from the committed payload): its C3a reads '+1.34/-0.60/+3.63 %' and its C3b 2024 reads '0.1769'; the SCORER'S OWN VALUES are C3a +1.36 / -0.61 / +3.61 % and C3b 0.1647 / 0.1762 / 0.1755. The two-decimal display had been rounded off the producing lane's report. Nothing else in the record moves and no verdict depends on the difference. THE RECORD: BUILT, ARMED AND SOLVED THROUGH THE AUTHORIZED CHANNEL ON AN OWNER INSTRUCTION ('first just tune the offer curve down by 7% across all fossil and launch an LP that runs that'); registered as 2026-09-09-spp-52a-fossil-offer. O not K because PROMOTION IS THE OWNER'S ACT and has not been ruled; O not R because the arm is live, C6 PASSES and nothing refutes it. PRECOMMIT-spp-52a-2026-09-09.md pushed at c1393878 BEFORE the solve. THE ARM: offer_curve_by_group committed/econ_low/econ_high/peak = 0.93 on the ten registered fossil classes SPP dispatches (CC_REGULAR, CC_CHP, CT_CHP, CT_PEAKER, ST_GAS, COAL, COAL_BIT, COAL_LIGNITE, COAL_PRB, COAL_WC). Verified in the run's own run_config: no phys_* field, no econ_low_share, no pct_peaking (CT_PEAKER keeps 0.526/7.0, COAL_PRB 0.55, ST_GAS 0.5/15.0), the three *_INTERMEDIATE curves untouched at peak 2.25/3.0/2.2, and ST_CHP EXCLUDED because it has no registered base curve and including it fails the launch with KeyError: 'econ_low_share' -- the price-family lane's own first-launch failure. ONE config across all three scored years, set ex ante by the owner and NEVER swept: exactly one multiplier was ever solved. Declared in the attestation's authorized_price_tuning block against the scorer's six-field schema, and carried as a ledgered free parameter (identification 'residual', sourced to the ruling; DOF n_residual 1 -> 2, entries unchanged at 3). MEASURED: load-weighted level -6.00/-5.91/-6.03 % -- FLAT TO 0.12 pp ACROSS THREE YEARS, which is the signature of a LEVEL lever and CONFIRMS the price-family lane's G-2 steepening refusal rather than overturning it. Nothing here rotates the stack and no shape claim is made. C3a +7.80/+5.64/+10.28 -> +1.34/-0.60/+3.63 %; C3b 0.1836/0.1894/0.2043 -> 0.1647/0.1769/0.1755. BOTH price criteria go from one failing year each to CLEAN IN ALL THREE YEARS -- the first SPP run for which C3a and C3b both PASS. C2/C4/C6/C8 PASS. The curtailment mechanism is unaffected (wind identity unchanged to five decimals; negative hours 229/214/167 vs 229/214/159). WHY THE R IS NOT SIMPLY REVERSED: the price-family lane's R was a refusal of a uniform quadruple AS A SHAPE REPAIR, and that refusal stands on its own G-2 evidence -- this arm reproduces it. What changed is the QUESTION: on keeper 4 the residual was a marginal LEVEL miss in one year (2025 +10.28 % against a +-10 % band), and a level lever is the apt instrument for a level miss. The basis also changed, since every price-family number was taken against the GMT-indexed actual SPP-51c repaired. REPORTED AGAINST THIS LANE'S INTEREST, both pre-registered: the determination does NOT change (NOT-YET) and a passing C3a is not a calibrated ISO. TWO criteria remain, both out of this channel's reach and both already routed: C1's 2024 ST_GAS row (-8.13 TWh, Harrington fuel vintage, SPP-46 R-4) and C3c in all three years (0/4/2 vs 42/59/68, SPP-55). ALSO A MISS OF THIS LANE'S OWN DECLARATION: the PRECOMMIT predicted the DOF ledger would reach '4 entries / 2 residual'; n_residual is right but the entry count stays 3, because the schema counts offer_curve_by_group as one entry carrying a dict, so arming the channel re-characterises an existing entry instead of adding one. And P-2's point predictions were each ~1 pp low because the realised level move is 6 %, not the assumed 7 %. THE STANDING-RULE OBSERVATION THE NEXT LANE SHOULD ACT ON: C3c is now the ONLY supporting-tier failure, so repairing the single C1 row would make C3c the LONE failure and the rubric v3.3 C3c standing rule would reclassify it to a ledgered caveat -- SPP would then read CALIBRATED. That makes SPP-46 R-4 (Harrington), not the thermal floor, the highest-value next lever. PRIOR EVIDENCE RETAINED: the price-family lane's G-2 kill (FINDING-spp-price-family-2026-09-07.md section 4) and SPP-51b's refusal of the channel on an hour census (the residual was a missing TAIL, and no multiplier makes a tail) both stand unamended." },
